From: AnacondaRecipes <noreply@anaconda.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Add default Culture metadata to ResourceCompile ItemDefinitionGroup

Newer MSBuild versions (post-VS17.10) require Culture metadata on
ResourceCompile items when other items in the same ItemGroup reference
%(Culture). Without it, MSBuild fires error MSB4096 in
Directory.vcxproj.targets when computing GITVER_LCID for ver.rc batch.

Combined with WiX's `-warnaserror` flag in dtf.cmd / burn.cmd /
ext/NetFx/netfx.cmd / etc., this aborts the entire build despite
SfxCA.dll and friends compiling successfully.

Set 0x0409 (en-US) as the default LCID for all ResourceCompile items.
This matches the pattern WiX upstream's CI relied on implicitly via an
older MSBuild that didn't enforce strict metadata propagation.

--- a/src/Directory.vcxproj.props
+++ b/src/Directory.vcxproj.props
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
     <ResourceCompile>
       <PreprocessorDefinitions>$(ArmPreprocessorDefinitions);%(PreprocessorDefinitions)</PreprocessorDefinitions>
       <AdditionalIncludeDirectories>$(ProjectAdditionalResourceIncludeDirectories);%(AdditionalIncludeDirectories)</AdditionalIncludeDirectories>
+      <Culture>0x0409</Culture>
     </ResourceCompile>
     <Lib>
       <AdditionalLibraryDirectories>$(OutDir);$(AdditionalMultiTargetLibraryPath);$(ProjectAdditionalLibraryDirectories);%(AdditionalLibraryDirectories)</AdditionalLibraryDirectories>
